 Terminal-style prompt history navigation for the DSH composer
 (ArrowUp/ArrowDown cycles through recently sent messages, persisted in
-localStorage), written in the 0.1.1-era style. The host is moving to
-dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2.
+localStorage), migrated to the dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2 client surface.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+- **↑ / ↓ history navigation in the composer**: ArrowUp walks to older sent
+  prompts, ArrowDown walks forward; past the newest entry the draft that was
+  being edited is restored.
+- **localStorage persistence**: the store is a FIFO list of unique prompts
+  (capacity 500), shared across sessions in the browser profile.
+- **Conversation-sourced history**: entries come from the current session's
+  `user` + `steering` conversation nodes, not from an input echo.
+- **Multi-line gate**: ArrowUp only fires from the first line, ArrowDown only
+  from the last line; elsewhere the editor keeps the arrow.
+- **IME safety**: keys during composition (including the Safari
+  post-`compositionend` keydown) are left to the editor.
+- **Slash/@ menu compatibility**: while a trigger menu is open, both arrows stay
+  with menu highlight navigation.
+- **Hero/blank-mode navigation**: the gesture is attached in the plugin's
+  `apply` body, so it stays live while the session renders as the hero and the
+  session-scoped dock is not mounted.
+
+## Migrated surface (dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2)
+
+| Concern | 0.1.1-era | 0.1.2-alpha.2 |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Composer surface | `<textarea>` located by `document.querySelector` | shell-owned Lexical contenteditable; the gesture uses the `ctx.conversation.composerKeys` seam, with `[data-composer-input]` only as the fallback anchor |
+| Draft write | native value setter + `input` event | `ctx.conversation.input.for(actx).setDraft(text)` |
+| Draft read | `textarea.value` | `InputState.draft` from that session's input facade |
+| Session resolution | renderer binding through `ctx.uiSession.adapter` | `ctx.sessions.list` current selection + `ctx.sessions.scope(id)` |
+| History source | `session.nodes` owner props | `useChat(s => s.legacy.nodes)` (Chat target nodes) |
+| Key listener | document bubble phase, `defaultPrevented` arbitration | the `composerKeys` offer (dispatched after trigger-menu arbitration); the fallback is a document **capture** listener whose consumed keys call `preventDefault` + `stopPropagation` |
+| Menu arbitration | `defaultPrevented` heuristic | done by the shell before the seam offer; the fallback asks `ctx.inputTriggers` `menu.open` and probes `[data-trigger-menu]` |
+| Dock entry | `conversation.composer.dock` (id, order 100) | unchanged — the slot still exists with the same id/order |
+
+The bundle layer (`cordis.patch.yml`) is unchanged and still required: it
+inserts the plugin row into the profile it is installed into.
+
+## Required harness patch
+
+`patches/composer-key-seam.patch` (slug `composer-key-seam`) adds the
+`ctx.conversation.composerKeys` registry to `dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2`, so a plugin can
+claim one composer arrow gesture after the trigger menu declines it and before
+the editor moves the caret. The plugin detects the registry and prefers it; on a
+build without it the capture-phase fallback keeps the documented gesture
+working. The patch is therefore required for the supported path, not for the
+plugin to run at all. Rationale, verification, and related upstream discussions
+live in `.dsh-migrate/patch-reports/composer-key-seam/report.md`.
 
