++# Agent Note: Composer key offers for client plugins
++
++Status: proposed
++
++English | [中文](2026-10-11-composer-key-plugin-offers.zh.md)
++
++## Problem
++
++The composer keymap owns ArrowUp/ArrowDown at `COMMAND_PRIORITY_CRITICAL`, and the only face carrying the editor's keyboard operations (`ComposerKeyboard`) is InputBar-exclusive by contract. A client plugin that needs one composer arrow gesture — terminal-style prompt-history recall is the concrete case — therefore has no extension point to register on: `ctx.conversation.input` covers draft reads and writes, but nothing offers the key. The workaround is a capture-phase `document` keydown listener plus the editor's undocumented DOM anchors, duplicating the shell's composition window and trigger-menu arbitration and breaking silently when the markup changes ([stable composer locator request](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/3981)). Community plugins ship the gesture this way, and the same user-facing request recurs ([input history in the Web composer](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/5031), [composer draft-history recall](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/6347), [ArrowUp prompt recall](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/1193)).
++
++## Proposal
++
++Add a root-scoped `ComposerKeys` registry to the public conversation service, reached as `ctx.conversation.composerKeys` and following `ctx.conversation.blocks`:
++
++- `register(handler)` returns a disposer; handlers run in registration order and the first `true` answer consumes the gesture.
++- The keymap raises the offer through the shell (`ComposerKeyboard.keystroke`) after `arbitrate` declines the key and before the plain-text caret move. A consumed offer calls `preventDefault()` and returns `true` from the Lexical command, exactly like a menu `consumed` verdict.
++- `ComposerKeyRequest` carries the gesture, the originating `KeyboardEvent`, the shell's composition state, and the composer's Session scope. The handler reads and writes that Session's draft through the existing `ctx.conversation.input` face instead of observing raw document keys.
++- Offers stop while the input is not `plain`; a claimed or submitting composer keeps every gesture until it settles.
++
++The registry's presence is the capability: a plugin that finds it must not also observe raw keydowns, and one running against a build without it keeps its own listener as the fallback path.
++
++The seam is additive to the [Web composer as a Lexical editor](../../implemented/architecture/2026-08-20-web-composer-lexical-editor.md) contract and the [Web input machine and slash pipeline](../../implemented/architecture/2026-07-25-web-input-machine-and-slash-pipeline.md): it offers a key the trigger pipeline already declined, and changes neither the submit plane nor the `slash/input-*` events. Neither note is superseded.
++
++## Alternatives considered
++
++**Scoped bail event (`conversation/composer-key`)**, matching `slash/input-*`. It loses on detection: a plugin cannot tell a build that dispatches the event from one that does not until a key arrives, so the fallback listener and the official path would both act on the first gesture, or the plugin would have to depend on a build that is not released.
++
++**Expose the editor or the `ComposerKeyboard` face to plugins.** It loses because the frozen contract is deliberately InputBar-exclusive; widening it hands every consumer the submit and trigger verbs the composer owns, instead of the one gesture a plugin needs.
++
++**Implement prompt recall in-tree instead** ([#1193](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/1193), [#6347](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/6347)). It loses because plugin-first composition leaves this product decision to plugins; the seam lets an in-tree recall and plugin implementations share one mechanism rather than choosing one and blocking the other.
++
++**Document the composer DOM anchors as stable surface** ([#3981](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/3981)). It removes the silent-breakage risk without new API, but leaves every consumer re-deriving composition state, menu arbitration, and caret gating that the shell already owns.
++
++## Acceptance criteria
++
++- `ctx.conversation.composerKeys.register(handler)` is reachable by a plugin that injects `conversation`; disposing the caller's fiber removes the offer.
++- A registered handler receives ArrowUp/ArrowDown with the originating event and the shell's composition state only when the trigger menu passed the key and the input phase is `plain`.
++- A `true` answer prevents the default and stops the editor's own caret move; a `false` answer leaves the gesture to `@lexical/plain-text`.
++- Existing trigger-menu, IME, Enter, Tab, and paste routing stay byte-compatible, and no plugin handler is reached for a key the menu consumed.
++
++## Risks
++
++- The offer sits on the composer's critical key path; a slow or throwing handler can delay or break typing. Handlers run synchronously with no completion promise, so a throw must be contained by the handler, as every plugin registration already assumes.
++- The Session-scope carrier admits untagged root listeners globally, so a handler registered at the root hears every Session's composer; the request carries the Session scope for resolution, but a handler that ignores it can write to the wrong Session.
++- The registry is additive surface on a 1.x-alpha client contract; once published it is held to the same compatibility promise as the rest of `IConversation`.
